IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clatas-dates`
IMPORT `clatas-common`
IMPORT `clatas-damages`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (Tas) -- baseline-2026-11: cases for clatas-common.l4 (ss 3B, 4) and clatas-damages.l4
-- (Parts 2, 3, 5, 5A, 7). Edges: each start date and the day before it; 6 and 7 months' imprisonment; 6 hours and 6
-- months; Amount A, Amount B and a dollar over each; the $250 rounding point; the 3 x AWE and 1/40 AWE caps.
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Cases -- what the Act reaches, and damages`

§§ `Short names`

`ordinary` MEANS `an ordinary claim: none of the s 3B exclusions`
`child abuse` MEANS `an intentional act that is child abuse within s 49J(3) (s 3B(1A))`
`intentional` MEANS `another intentional act done with intent to cause injury or death, or sexual assault or other sexual misconduct (s 3B(1)(a))`
`tobacco` MEANS `personal injury or death that resulted from smoking or other use of tobacco products (s 3B(1)(b))`
`motor` MEANS `an injury Part III of the Motor Accidents (Liabilities and Compensation) Act 1973 applies to (s 3B(2))`
`work injury` MEANS `an injury Division 2 of Part X of the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 applies to (s 3B(3))`
`scheme` MEANS `compensation under the workers compensation, asbestos diseases, criminal injuries or anti-discrimination Acts, or a motor accidents scheduled benefit (s 3B(4))`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`2010` MEANS d 1 6 2010

§§ `ss 3B, 4 -- does the Part apply`

`applies` MEANS `Does this Part of the Act apply to my claim`

#ASSERT applies `Part 7 (assessment of damages), other than ss 28A to 28D and 28BA` `ordinary` (d 4 7 2003) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT applies `Part 7 (assessment of damages), other than ss 28A to 28D and 28BA` `ordinary` (d 3 7 2003) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 7 (assessment of damages), other than ss 28A to 28D and 28BA` `motor` `2010` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT applies `Part 9 (public and other authorities)` `motor` `2010` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 6 Divisions 5 and 6 (dangerous recreational activities, professional negligence)` `motor` `2010` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 4 (apologies)` `motor` `2010` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 7 (assessment of damages), other than ss 28A to 28D and 28BA` `child abuse` `2010` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 10C (child abuse, liability of organisations)` `child abuse` `2010` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT applies `Part 4 (apologies)` `child abuse` `2010` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT applies `Part 10C (child abuse, liability of organisations)` `intentional` `2010` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 7 (assessment of damages), other than ss 28A to 28D and 28BA` `work injury` `2010` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 5 (structured settlements)` `scheme` `2010` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 3 (recovery by criminals)` `ordinary` `2010` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 5 (structured settlements)` `ordinary` (d 1 1 1999) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT applies `Part 9A (proportionate liability)` `ordinary` (d 31 5 2005) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 9A (proportionate liability)` `ordinary` (d 1 6 2005) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT applies `Part 8A (good samaritans)` `ordinary` (d 21 10 2008) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 8B (food donors)` `ordinary` (d 22 10 2008) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT applies `Part 10B (employer and employee)` `ordinary` (d 29 5 2012) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `Part 10B (employer and employee)` `ordinary` (d 30 5 2012) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT applies `s 28BA (loss of capacity to provide gratuitous services)` `ordinary` (d 28 2 2014) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT applies `s 28BA (loss of capacity to provide gratuitous services)` `ordinary` (d 1 3 2014) FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `s 5 -- intoxication`

-- Arguments: kind; accrued before the Act; under the influence; medicinal and unaware; capacity impaired; not
-- self-induced; did not contribute; another percentage; that percentage.
`intox` MEANS `By how much will my damages be reduced for intoxication`

#ASSERT intox `ordinary` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT intox `ordinary` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 40 EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT intox `ordinary` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 EQUALS JUST 10
-- A Part III motor accident claim keeps Part 2 (s 3B(2)).
#ASSERT intox `motor` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT intox `work injury` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT intox `ordinary` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(6): a medicinal drug whose effect the person was unaware of.
#ASSERT intox `ordinary` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(4): not self-induced.
#ASSERT intox `ordinary` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(1) "unless": the intoxication did not contribute.
#ASSERT intox `ordinary` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Capacity not impaired; not under the influence.
#ASSERT intox `ordinary` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT intox `ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

`after` MEANS `How much are my damages after the intoxication reduction`
#ASSERT after 100000 (JUST 25) EQUALS JUST 75000
#ASSERT after 80000 (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 48000
#ASSERT after 100000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 6 -- recovery by criminals`

-- Arguments: kind; accrued before the Act; court satisfied of the offence; maximum months; contributed materially.
`crime` MEANS `Can I be awarded damages despite my offence`

#ASSERT crime `ordinary` FALSE TRUE 24 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT crime `ordinary` FALSE TRUE 7 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 6 months is not "greater than 6 months".
#ASSERT crime `ordinary` FALSE TRUE 6 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT crime `ordinary` FALSE TRUE 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT crime `ordinary` FALSE TRUE 24 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT crime `ordinary` FALSE FALSE 24 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT crime `ordinary` TRUE TRUE 24 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT crime `motor` FALSE TRUE 24 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT crime `tobacco` FALSE TRUE 24 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8 -- structured settlements`

`structured` MEANS `Can the court approve my structured settlement`
#ASSERT structured `ordinary` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT structured `motor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT structured `ordinary` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT structured `ordinary` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT structured `work injury` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8B -- provisional damages`

`dust` MEANS `Is my condition a dust-related disease`
#ASSERT dust asbestosis EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT dust mesothelioma EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT dust talcosis EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT dust `another condition of the lung, pleura or peritoneum attributable to dust` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT dust `another condition` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: kind; condition; proved or admitted; commenced before 1 March 2014; hearing, award or settlement by then.
`provisional` MEANS `Can the court award me provisional damages`
#ASSERT provisional `ordinary` mesothelioma TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT provisional `ordinary` silicosis FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT provisional `ordinary` `another condition` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(2A), (2B): an older action is reached unless it had got to a hearing, award or settlement by 1 March 2014.
#ASSERT provisional `ordinary` asbestosis TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT provisional `ordinary` asbestosis TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT provisional `motor` asbestosis TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT provisional `tobacco` `asbestos-induced carcinoma` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT provisional `scheme` asbestosis TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 25 -- superannuation`

`super` MEANS `What is the most I can be awarded for lost superannuation`
#ASSERT super `ordinary` `2010` 100000 12 EQUALS JUST 12000
#ASSERT super `ordinary` `2010` 250000 9.5 EQUALS JUST 23750
#ASSERT super `ordinary` (d 3 7 2003) 100000 12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT super `tobacco` `2010` 100000 12 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 26 -- earning capacity`

`earnings` MEANS `On what weekly earnings can my damages be based`
-- AWE $2 000 a week: the cap is $6 000.
#ASSERT earnings `ordinary` `2010` 7000 2000 EQUALS JUST 6000
#ASSERT earnings `ordinary` `2010` 6000 2000 EQUALS JUST 6000
#ASSERT earnings `ordinary` `2010` 6001 2000 EQUALS JUST 6000
#ASSERT earnings `ordinary` `2010` 5000 2000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT earnings `motor` `2010` 7000 2000 EQUALS JUST 6000
#ASSERT earnings `work injury` `2010` 7000 2000 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 27 -- non-economic loss`

`Amount A` MEANS `What is Amount A`
#ASSERT `Amount A` 2003 0 1 EQUALS JUST 4000
#ASSERT `Amount A` 2002 150 80 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 4000 x 150 / 80 = 7500, a multiple of 500.
#ASSERT `Amount A` 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 7500
-- 4000 x 145 / 80 = 7250: $250 over a multiple rounds up.
#ASSERT `Amount A` 2026 145 80 EQUALS JUST 7500
-- 4000 x 144.99 / 80 = 7249.50: rounds down.
#ASSERT `Amount A` 2026 144.99 80 EQUALS JUST 7000
-- 4000 x 80 / 80 = 4000.
#ASSERT `Amount A` 2004 80 80 EQUALS JUST 4000
-- 4000 x 130 / 80 = 6500.
#ASSERT `Amount A` 2015 130 80 EQUALS JUST 6500

-- Amount A $7 500, Amount B $37 500 (2026, CPI 150 over 80).
`nel` MEANS `How much will I be awarded for non-economic loss`
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` `2010` 7500 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` `2010` 5000 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` `2010` 7501 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 1.25
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` `2010` 20000 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 15625
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` `2010` 37500 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 37500
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` `2010` 37501 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 37501
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` `2010` 100000 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 100000
-- 2003-04: Amount A $4 000, Amount B $20 000; 1.25 x (12 000 - 4 000) = 10 000.
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` (d 4 7 2003) 12000 2003 0 1 EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` (d 3 7 2003) 12000 2003 0 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT nel `motor` `2010` 20000 2026 150 80 EQUALS JUST 15625
#ASSERT nel `intentional` `2010` 20000 2026 150 80 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT nel `ordinary` `2010` 20000 2002 150 80 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 28A -- discount rate`

`discount` MEANS `What discount rate applies to my future loss`
#ASSERT discount `ordinary` `2010` TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT discount `ordinary` `2010` TRUE TRUE 3 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT discount `ordinary` `2010` FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT discount `ordinary` (d 15 12 2005) TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT discount `ordinary` (d 14 12 2005) TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT discount `motor` `2010` TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 5

§§ `ss 28B, 28C -- gratuitous services`

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; needed because of another's negligence; hours a week; consecutive months.
`services` MEANS `Can I recover damages for gratuitous services`
#ASSERT services `ordinary` `2010` TRUE 7 7 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT services `ordinary` `2010` TRUE 6 12 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT services `ordinary` `2010` TRUE 6.5 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT services `ordinary` `2010` TRUE 20 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT services `ordinary` `2010` FALSE 20 12 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 28C: never in a Part III motor accident claim.
#ASSERT services `motor` `2010` TRUE 20 12 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT services `ordinary` (d 14 12 2005) TRUE 20 12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT services `ordinary` (d 15 12 2005) TRUE 20 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT services `work injury` `2010` TRUE 20 12 EQUALS NOTHING

-- AWE $2 000: the hourly cap is $50, the weekly cap $2 000.
`weekly` MEANS `What is the most a week for gratuitous services`
#ASSERT weekly 10 40 2000 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT weekly 10 60 2000 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT weekly 40 50 2000 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT weekly 50 50 2000 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT weekly 50 30 2000 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT weekly 70 30 2000 EQUALS 2000

§§ `ss 28BA, 28C -- loss of capacity to care for another`

-- Arguments: kind; accrual; unborn child; hours; months; necessary; could claim had I been killed; would have kept
-- providing; will reasonably need.
`care` MEANS `Can I recover damages for my lost capacity to care for another`
#ASSERT care `ordinary` `2015` FALSE 20 24 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT care `ordinary` `2015` FALSE 6 24 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT care `ordinary` `2015` FALSE 20 6 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT care `ordinary` `2015` FALSE 20 24 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An unborn child: the hours and months before the injury do not matter.
#ASSERT care `ordinary` `2015` TRUE 0 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT care `ordinary` `2015` FALSE 20 24 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT care `ordinary` `2015` FALSE 20 24 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT care `ordinary` `2015` FALSE 20 24 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT care `motor` `2015` FALSE 20 24 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT care `ordinary` (d 28 2 2014) FALSE 20 24 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT care `ordinary` (d 1 3 2014) FALSE 20 24 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

`2015` MEANS d 1 6 2015

§§ `ss 28D, 28E -- consortium and abolished actions`

`action` MEANS `Can I bring this action`
#ASSERT action `ordinary` `2010` `loss or impairment of the consortium of my spouse or significant partner` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT action `ordinary` (d 14 12 2005) `loss or impairment of the consortium of my spouse or significant partner` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT action `motor` `2010` `loss or impairment of the consortium of my spouse or significant partner` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT action `ordinary` `2010` seduction EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT action `ordinary` (d 1 1 1990) champerty EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT action `ordinary` (d 4 7 2003) champerty EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT action `ordinary` (d 3 7 2003) maintenance EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT action `ordinary` `2010` harbouring EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT action `ordinary` `2010` `another action` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT action `intentional` `2010` enticement EQUALS NOTHING
